        "imagePath": "media/Tokens/PC-William.webp",
        "description": "Impatient, loud-mouthed teen... who shouldn't be here",
        "backstory": "You are not who people think you are. Your real name is Joclyn Corolinus, Princess of Arvey and heir to the House of Four Chambers. But you are sick of the gossip, the dancing, and the diplomatic dinners. Your elven grandmother was a warrior, and you loved her stories of skirmishes against the orcs and hobgoblins of Zarak. Surely her blood runs strong in your veins! You've won the archery contest three years in a row! So when you heard that Arvey was forming a war party to hunt down that brigand and murderer Fat Farlsbag, you decided to join. Scissors to your hair, scale armor from the guardroom, you fit right in. Although you've had to keep a low profile since you saw that your cousin, Count Conrad, was in the war party and looking for you..",
        "dmNotes": "The PDF prints the name as \"Wiliam Exel\" — the pregen pages' font drops one letter of every doubled \"ll\", so the printed name is William Exel (the same artifact turns \"all\" into \"al\" and \"well\" into \"wel\" throughout those pages).\n\nThe PDF prints only this name, the one-line hook and the backstory above — no ability scores, class, level, hit points or gear. The scale armor is from the backstory (\"scale armor from the guardroom\"), as is the archery. The 2nd-level ranger build is a suggestion; swap it freely.\n\nJoclyn's cousin is @[Count Conrad Mannheim](entity:npc/Count Conrad Mannheim), the dying hostage in Fat Farlsbag's camp — a ready-made hook if the party rescues him."
      }
    }
